  "articleBody": "Deciding to convert your garage into an Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU) is a big step, and picking the right contractor is crucial for a smooth process and a successful outcome. You want someone who understands the ins and outs of ADU conversions in the Bay Area, especially with all the specific regulations and potential challenges. Don't just go with the first quote; ask smart questions that reveal their expertise and how they'll handle your unique project.\n\n### Questions to Ask Before You Decide\nWhen you're interviewing potential contractors, make sure to dig into their experience with ADU conversions specifically. Ask if they're familiar with the building department in your specific city or county, as requirements can differ significantly. It's really helpful to see examples of their completed ADU conversion projects, especially ones similar to what you're envisioning for your garage. You should also clarify what their permit and inspection scope includes – will they handle everything from application to closeout? A good contractor will conduct a thorough site investigation, looking for things like foundation issues, unpermitted prior work, or utility conflicts that could complicate things. Get a detailed, itemized pricing breakdown and understand what's excluded from their quote, as well as their approach to change orders. Lastly, confirm their responsibility for corrections if any issues arise during or after construction. You want a team that prioritizes clear communication and dependable coordination, just like Hometelligent Inc. has done for homeowners in the East Bay for decades. Remember, California HCD's handbook and your local building department's guidelines should always be the ultimate authority over any contractor's claims.\n\nReady to get started? Contact Hometelligent Inc. today for an expert consultation on your garage conversion ADU project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-27"
}